---
// Security headers are set at the edge, by the Cloudflare Transform Rule on the
// tinnova.com.br zone (ruleset 865df0efa19d4f5fad5bf75df6471e25).
//
// The CSP used to live here as a <meta> because GitHub Pages cannot set response
// headers. The apex is now proxied through Cloudflare, so the policy ships as a
// real header: frame-ancestors and report-uri actually work (both are ignored in
// a meta CSP), it covers non-HTML responses, and it can change without a deploy.
//
// Do NOT add a <meta> CSP back here. Browsers enforce every policy they receive,
// so a meta tag would apply on top of the edge policy as an intersection, and the
// stricter of the two wins — silently overriding the rule in Cloudflare.
//
// IMPORTANT: adding a GTM tag that loads a script from a new domain now means
// adding that domain to script-src in the Cloudflare rule, not in this file.
//
// Set at the edge: Content-Security-Policy, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy,
// Permissions-Policy, Strict-Transport-Security, X-Content-Type-Options.
---
<meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin">
